  {
    "field_name": "Validation Objective",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Validates local and remote numa_sweep latency. On one node, remote may equal local"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Command Execution Details and Purpose",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Build src/numa_sweep.cpp and run a stride-64 pointer chase on yaml local and remote NUMA targets for each working_set_size, optionally under perf stat -e cache-misses, to measure local versus remote latency, cross-socket ratio, bandwidth, and miss rate. collect_numa_cache.py writes those metrics into the harness raw file"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Command Methodology",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Build src/numa_sweep.cpp and run a stride-64 pointer chase on yaml local and remote NUMA targets for each working_set_size, optionally under perf stat -e cache-misses. Record local versus remote latency, cross-socket ratio, bandwidth, and miss rate. collect_numa_cache.py writes those metrics into the harness raw file"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Execution Description With Parameters",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "Builds src/numa_sweep.cpp and runs scripts/collect_numa_cache.py (dispatched by scripts/collect_workload.py) for local/remote working-set sizes. source_numa_node/target_numa_node: intended bind pair (yaml 0 versus 0,remote). working_set_size: swept footprints. num_threads, page_size, cache_level, access_pattern, stride, and num_iterations come from yaml. Optional perf stat -e cache-misses may record 0 if perf_event_open is blocked; numactl mempolicy falls back if the container denies it. The overlay writes the full METRICS_CSV (local/remote latency, cross-socket ratio, bandwidth, and cache-misses) into the raw file; the harness does not strip the file to latency-only columns"
  },
